ates the Wait Bar as a context manager.\n   579→\n   580→        If the Wait Bar is already active, then its message is updated for the new\n   581→        context. Once the new context is complete, the previous Wait Bar message\n   582→        is restored.\n   583→\n   584→        :param message: text explaining what is being awaited; should end in '...'\n   585→        :param done_message: text appended to the message after exiting\n   586→        :param transient: if True, remove bar and message from screen after exiting;\n   587→            if False (default), the message will remain on the screen without pulsing bar.\n   588→        :param markup: whether to interpret Rich styling markup in the message; if True,\n   589→            the message must already be escaped; defaults False.\n   590→        :returns:  Keep-alive spinner to notify user Briefcase is still waiting\n   591→        \"\"\"\n   592→        is_wait_bar_disabled = not self.is_interactive\n   593→        show_outcome_message = message and (is_wait_bar_disabled or not transient)\n   594→\n   595→        if self._wait_bar is None:\n   596→            self._wait_bar = Progress(\n   597→                TextColumn(\"    \"),\n   598→                BarColumn(bar_width=20, style=\"black\", pulse_style=\"white\"),\n   599→                TextColumn(\"{task.fields[message]}\"),\n   600→                transient=True,\n   601→                disable=is_wait_bar_disabled,\n   602→                console=self.print.console,\n   603→            )\n   604→            # start=False causes the progress bar to \"pulse\"\n   605→            # message=None is a sentinel the Wait Bar should be inactive\n   606→            self._wait_bar.add_task(\"\", start=False, message=None)\n   607→\n   608→        self.print(\n   609→            f\"{message} started\", markup=markup, show=message and is_wait_bar_disabled\n   610→        )\n   611→\n   612→        self.is_console_controlled = True\n   613→        wait_bar_task